A||||2||Johnson's85SE||Outside Door handle||||11||
Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||12-07-2000||06:24 PM||||It was a mild October day. I washed and waxed my black fiero. Little did I know the -15 celceous evening was quickly approaching. The next morning both my doors were frozen shut, a common Calgary Winter cliche. In my haste, (Quick, uncontrolled, SPAZ) I broke the fiberglass between the outside handle and the outer door skin. I took it all apart on the inside, and with the power window up, squeesed my hand inside above the lock bar to see if the two bolts were still tight. To take off the outside handle you must take out the two bolts. I can't get my hand in there, let alone a cresent wrench. Any suggestions? Thanks, for listening to my wine.<BR>Chris  <P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||11
Z||000001||Tigger||12-07-2000||08:45 PM||||There's a nylon clip that holds the handle to the linkage.  Unsnap it from the linkage and the rod will release.  No other way at getting at those two nuts that hold the handle.  Small socket wrench and I believe it takes a 10 mm socket.  I would think a cresent wrench should get in there.  If you have power locks you have a lot less room to work with.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||12-07-2000||08:53 PM||||if you're talking about the 2 nuts that aren't really nuts, i used an 11mm on those. sounds weird, but it fits. unless this is just some weirdness on my car.<BR>by the way, welcome to the forum.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
